Everyone does. Sugar lights up the same reward parts of your brain, at the same intensity, as cocaine. It is immediate, easy to digest energy, and in the wild it *should* be the first thing we go eat when given a choice. The problem is that it's in everything and we add sugar to things until we hit a "bliss point" (look it up) where any more sugar makes things taste worse. The entire processed foods industry basically is hitting you with maximum sweetness and maximum sugar to give you maximum happiness in the act of consumption and it impacts your palate and your health.

&nbsp;

It takes about two weeks to physically withdraw from sugar. At that point you still get cravings but they're more psychological than physical. After five or six weeks those fade away.

