&gt; (today i went a little over, 20g net, oops) 

You're fine I promise. the 20g is a rule of thumb meant to shoot low enough that you're certainly in ketosis without having to use a blood meter or something like that. When I started keto, everyone said 25 grams of net carbs a day was a good rule of thumb, and that most people enter ketosis under 50 grams of net carbs per day. Everyone is different, and your carb tolerance will be a little different. I aim for 25, but I know in reality I can usually hit around 35 and still be in ketosis reliably. Aim low and if you slop over a little bit you're still fine. 

