If you're in the states you can go get a rotisserie chicken for like 5 bucks from a large retailer or other markets. When I don't want to cook I do the rotisserie thing. I also have a microwave steamer tray and will buy some green beans or broccoli or cauliflower or frozen veg mix and steam that, then maybe hit with a drizzle of sesame oil to jazz it up a little. Takes less than 5 minutes to steam veggies in the microwave, and the rotisserie chicken is good for a meal or two. Once it's done if you're in the mood you can throw it into a pressure cooker/instant pot/slow cooker and make some chicken stock out of it and feel really industrious. 

