One of my comfort foods is tomato soup. Get 1 28 oz can of whole peeled tomatoes, dump into pot. Add 4-5 tablespoons butter, 1/2 of an onion chopped roughly, 1 1/2 cups of chicken stock, vegetable stock, or water. Salt &amp; pepper a little, then let simmer for 45 minutes. Blend with an immersion blender or pour into a blender and blitz in batches. Add a few tablespoons of cream if you want a bisque. Season to taste with salt &amp; pepper, maybe some sugar if the tomatoes have that canned flavor. A very low effort, incredibly tasty tomato soup. Add BLT or grilled cheese sammich, or some real bacon bacon bits and a side salad.

